# STGST00A room — scene composition manifest (native-port host data).
#
# This file is NOT extracted game data. It is the host-side seam where the
# semantic KanbanSceneLoader acquires the real room geometry that the renderer
# draws for a scene. sceneId 0x0F is the dominant world_state observed in the
# runtime capture (Rev.104: ws=0x0F -> 429,907 ios_om_main events, 58.1%,
# single slot B dispatch). The world_state-to-scene mapping itself is NOT
# confirmed; this manifest binds sceneId 0x0F to the STGST00A pieces purely as
# host test data so the renderer has a deterministic room to exercise.
#
# Pieces are the same 28 files the demo previously hardcoded in main.cpp's
# kOrder; the renderer now consumes this manifest through KanbanSceneLoader
# instead of a baked-in list.
#
# scene 0x2B reuses the same host piece library purely as host test data so
# the role-driven re-link test (gobj_attachment_test, Rev.159) has a room
# whose verified runtime handler repertoire (GeneratedRoomRoleTables.h) drives
# the GObjHandle->handler binding. It does NOT claim these pieces compose the
# original scene 0x2B room.
#
# Paths are relative to this file's directory.

texturedir texture
piecesdir pieces

scene 0x0F
  169_door.p2o
  170_st00a_p1.p2o
  171_st00a_p2.p2o
  172_st00a_torch1_add.p2o
  173_st00a_torch2_add.p2o
  174_st00a_torch3_add.p2o
  175_st00a_window_flare.p2o
  176_st00a_window_glow.p2o
